      "notes": "SEND BACK. Rulings. MEDIAN OF 42 FETCHED RESULTS · 535: the figure is history (results from 2 October to 12 November, before this window) and is the aggregate the screen's ruling 8 allows; it does not count this week's results. As staged it reads as history only if the date line under it is read, and that line is too faint (reasons). The counter: the roll from 2,648 to 1 takes 0.74 s and every frame of it is labelled POSTS under SATURDAY and the bot's tag, the 201 frame included; the label must come off while the number moves (reasons). The arithmetic clearing at 89.05 s, before \"Still.\": passes; the header EPPY'S GUESS · NOT A RESULT is up from 76.3 s to the last frame, so the guess is labelled for as long as it is made and the one word has the board to itself. Against ruling 8: one named winner (CEE, @cee.wtf, and the same name under the record bar once the post is read); two other scores (440, 366) on crowns with no name and no day; the withheld result is in no form here, not as a score, a share, a gap, a rank or a blank; no leaderboard and nothing below the record line; the bot is tagged SCORED BY A BOT · UNOFFICIAL and its card BOT · UNOFFICIAL RANKINGS; no weekday marker in the market block; the market is a STUDIO SKETCH with its address and no \"by\"; NO REAL MONEY is a plain header. All five cards match the digest in text, cuts, dates and counts; the winning post's 222 likes carry the tag 201 AT THE RESULT. The desk's own lettering (THE LATE CLUSTER) sits under the caption box in every desk frame and shows cut off beside it; that is the studio's desk and caption position, not this segment's file."
