      "notes": "SEND BACK. Rulings. The see-through lap: a cold viewer will read \"underneath\" (the flag hangs upside down and Larry leans to look), but will not see every square go gold on both faces, because the gold already laid appears to be taken away when the view changes, and again for a moment when it changes back. The turn needs gold only ever to grow. The one view meant to show both faces gold, the last turn at 51.9 to 53.5 s, is in full for about a third of a second, and in it the upper face is again only a dashed outline. The twist: at the front, in every shot of the board. No rule is shown and no piece moves; the only thing that travels is the flag, which is labelled Larry's. The footer running again at this segment's first guest: keep it; it costs nothing and a clip of the last segment carries it. The maker's display name: exact on the card; the chyron and the credits put it in capitals as they do every name, with the exact form on the card beside it. The wordless stretch, 41.2 to 53.0 s: meets the measure; frames at 42.4, 47.4 and 51.4 s show the flag setting off, under the board, and home on gold; they differ; STUDIO SKETCH and the credit ringmate · mobius.mokkenstorm.dev · by @mokkenstorm.dev are on all three; the only text is four name flags. The cards gate did not cover this segment: all three cards match the digest in text, dates and counts. Both guests' chyrons carry PUPPET · PARODY. The close: Sibyl turns to the camera on the last line and the board stays as it was left; her caption box sits over the twist for those four lines, which is minor. The end card: it names the six real accounts by display name and handle under PUPPETS PLAYED THE POSTING PERSONAS OF, says EVERY VOICE IN THIS PROGRAMME IS SYNTHESIZED BY CHIMERA, and credits the synth and its author; handles are readable; that part passes. One line of the roll does not (reasons)."
